      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The fight against pain in children has progressed significantly since the 1980s. The setting up of pain prevention plans, the issuing of good practice recommendations, the development of new treatments as well as the training of professionals in particular account for this progress. However, caregivers must remain vigilant in order that the quality of care provided to a child in pain remains a priority."},
